  [PASS] C3b  eta=50 (very strong external field): gamma_v -> 1.000, EFE vanishes -> matches DARK-MATTER / GR baseline
        gamma_v(eta=50) = 1.0000000000, mu_e=1.0000000000
  [PASS] C3c  eta=1e-4 (deep-MOND EFD): q -> 2.000 (the standard deep-MOND external-field anisotropy)
        q(eta=1e-4) = 1.999950
  [PASS] C4  internal boost is monotonically DECREASING in g_ext (stronger host field -> more Newtonised) -- the EFE sign
        gamma_v(||) at eta=[0.3,1,1.9,4,10] = 1.964, 1.258, 1.084, 1.009, 1.000
======================================================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE EFE LAW (exponential kernel), both footings
======================================================================================================================
  EFD (external-field-dominated, g_ext > g_in) internal equation:
      mu_e (d_x^2 + d_y^2 + q d_z^2) phi = 4 pi G rho ,   mu_e = 1 - e^{-eta}, eta = g_ext/a0
      q = 1 + L_e ,  L_e = eta/(e^eta - 1)
  Directional velocity-boost gamma_v^2 = G_eff/G:
      || g_ext (radial):  gamma_v^2 = 1/mu_e
      _|_ g_ext        :  gamma_v^2 = 1/(mu_e sqrt(q))

  [canonical] eta=1.8992  mu_e=0.8503  L_e=0.3343  q=1.3343
              gamma_v:  || = 1.0845   _|_ = 1.0090   orientation-avg = 1.0326
              SEP-violation amplitude (orient-avg): gamma_v - 1 = 0.0326  (3.26%)
              intrinsic anisotropy spread || vs _|_ : 0.0754 in gamma_v
  [alt      ] eta=1.5764  mu_e=0.7933  L_e=0.4108  q=1.4108
              gamma_v:  || = 1.1228   _|_ = 1.0302   orientation-avg = 1.0588
              SEP-violation amplitude (orient-avg): gamma_v - 1 = 0.0588  (5.88%)
              intrinsic anisotropy spread || vs _|_ : 0.0926 in gamma_v
