PART 2 -- WIDE BINARIES: F(Q)Theta EFE gamma_v vs registered DR4 band
======================================================================================================================
  Observable: deep-regime velocity-boost gamma_v (gravity boost G_eff/G = gamma_v^2).
  Registered DR4 targets (frozen literals, read-only):
      ARM A (modified-GRAVITY, framework nu_RAR): (1.1614, 1.1814) canonical / (1.1917, 1.2267) alt ; edge 1.23
      ARM B (covariant candidate CEILINGS, killed-from-above): 1.045 can / 1.03 alt
      superseded per-star MI: 1.1582   ;  conventional-MOND benchmark: 1.33
      Chae et al. detections (gamma_v): 1.19-1.26

  [canonical] F(Q)Theta exponential-kernel gamma_v (orient-avg) = 1.0326  [range _|_..|| = 1.0090..1.0845]
              vs Arm A band (1.1614, 1.1814):  BELOW lower edge by 0.1288 in gamma_v
              vs Arm B ceiling 1.045:  gamma_v is <= ceiling (diff -0.0124)
  [alt      ] F(Q)Theta exponential-kernel gamma_v (orient-avg) = 1.0588  [range _|_..|| = 1.0302..1.1228]
              vs Arm A band (1.1917, 1.2267):  BELOW lower edge by 0.1329 in gamma_v
              vs Arm B ceiling 1.03:  gamma_v is > ceiling (diff +0.0288)

  WHY below Arm A (the D1 kernel conflict, quantified): the exponential mu=1-e^{-y}
  Newtonises FASTER at y~1.9 than nu_RAR, so its EFD mu_e is closer to 1 (smaller boost).
      [canonical] exponential mu_e = 0.8503  vs  Arm A implied mu_eff ~ 0.7414   (nu_RAR is 'more MOND': mu_eff < mu_e)
      [alt      ] exponential mu_e = 0.7933  vs  Arm A implied mu_eff ~ 0.7042   (nu_RAR is 'more MOND': mu_eff < mu_e)
  [PASS] P2a  F(Q)Theta predicts a NONZERO wide-binary EFE (gamma_v>1) on both footings -- a SEP violation DM does not produce
  [PASS] P2b  exponential-kernel gamma_v is BELOW the registered Arm A (nu_RAR modified-gravity) band on BOTH footings
        canonical 1.0326 < 1.1614 ; alt 1.0588 < 1.1917  => the kernel that actually descends from F(Q)Theta does NOT predict the registered Arm A signal
  [PASS] P2c  exponential gamma_v sits in the Arm-B / near-Newton band (consistent with covariant-candidate ceilings & Newton-leaning WB analyses)
        canonical 1.0326 vs ceil 1.045 ; alt 1.0588 vs ceil 1.03

  DETECTABILITY (honest): gamma_v ~ 1.03-1.06 is only 3-6% above Newton (1.000), FAR weaker than the
  nu_RAR Arm A signal (16-23%).  Wide binaries are therefore a WEAK discriminator for the exponential
  kernel: separating 1.03 from 1.00 at 3 sigma needs ~10x more deep pairs than separating 1.16 from 1.00.
  [PASS] P2d  the exponential prediction is INCONSISTENT with Chae et al.'s central detection (gamma_v 1.19-1.26); it matches the Newton-leaning (Pittordis-Sutherland/Banik) analyses instead -- and the WB EFE is observationally CONTESTED
        exponential canonical 1.0326 vs Chae (1.19, 1.26)
