PART 3 -- DWARF SPHEROIDALS: internal sigma depends on Galactocentric distance (DM does not)
======================================================================================================================
  Fiducial dwarf: M_baryon = 1e6 Msun, r_half = 300 pc.  MW field g_ext(R) = Vc^2/R, Vc = 180 km/s.
  Predictions of the 1-D velocity dispersion (structure const k=3 in sigma^2 = G_eff M/(k r_half)):
    - Newton (baryons only):    sigma_N   = sqrt(G M/(k r_half))
    - isolated deep-MOND:       sigma_iso = ((4/9) G M a0)^{1/4}   (no EFE)
    - MOND + EFE (EFD):         sigma_EFE = sigma_N / sqrt(mu_e(g_ext(R)/a0)),  capped at sigma_iso

  dwarf internal field g_in = GM/r_half^2 = 1.549e-12 m/s^2 = 0.0165 a0_can (deep-MOND internally)
  [canonical] sigma_N = 2.186 km/s   sigma_iso(no-EFE) = 8.621 km/s   g_ext=g_in at R = 678 kpc
             R_gc[kpc]   g_ext/a0    mu_e     sigma_EFE[km/s]
                   40      0.2804   0.2445       4.421
                   80      0.1402   0.1308       6.045
                  160      0.0701   0.0677       8.403
                  250      0.0449   0.0439       8.621
             => sigma_EFE varies 4.421 -> 8.621 km/s across 40->250 kpc (factor 1.95); DM predicts a FLAT sigma(R_gc).
  [alt      ] sigma_N = 2.186 km/s   sigma_iso(no-EFE) = 9.032 km/s   g_ext=g_in at R = 678 kpc
             R_gc[kpc]   g_ext/a0    mu_e     sigma_EFE[km/s]
                   40      0.2327   0.2076       4.798
                   80      0.1164   0.1099       6.596
                  160      0.0582   0.0565       9.032
                  250      0.0372   0.0366       9.032
             => sigma_EFE varies 4.798 -> 9.032 km/s across 40->250 kpc (factor 1.88); DM predicts a FLAT sigma(R_gc).

  Touchstone -- Crater II (McGaugh 2016; MOND EFE predicted its anomalously LOW sigma):
    [canonical] isolated-MOND sigma = 6.86 km/s ; EFE-suppressed sigma = 2.39 km/s  (obs ~ 2.7 km/s)  => EFE pulls the prediction DOWN toward the low observed value
    [alt      ] isolated-MOND sigma = 7.18 km/s ; EFE-suppressed sigma = 2.61 km/s  (obs ~ 2.7 km/s)  => EFE pulls the prediction DOWN toward the low observed value
  [PASS] P3a  F(Q)Theta predicts dwarf internal sigma RISES with Galactocentric distance (~factor 2 over 40-250 kpc); cold DM predicts ZERO R_gc-dependence -- a clean, DM-distinguishing test
  [PASS] P3b  the EFE SUPPRESSES sigma of dwarfs deep in the MW field (small R_gc), consistent with the low sigma of Crater II -- the DM interpretation must invoke tides/stripping instead
======================================================================================================================
PART 4 -- CRISP FALSIFIABLE STATEMENT + verdict
======================================================================================================================
  F(Q)Theta (exponential kernel) predicts a SPECIFIC, NONZERO EFE (SEP violation):
    (1) WIDE BINARIES @2-30 kAU, g_ext=1.9/1.58 a0:
          orientation-avg gamma_v = 1.033 (canonical) / 1.059 (alt)
          anisotropic: gamma_v(||g_ext) = 1.084/1.123, gamma_v(_|_) = 1.009/1.030
    (2) DWARF SPHEROIDALS: internal sigma proportional to ~sqrt(R_gc) in the EFD regime -> ~2x across the
          satellite distance range; specifically LOW sigma for dwarfs deep in the MW field (Crater II-like).
    DARK MATTER predicts: gamma_v = 1.000 (no SEP violation) AND sigma independent of R_gc.

  DECISIVE TEST:
    - CLEANEST: the dwarf sigma-vs-R_gc correlation (a ~2x effect, well above measurement error for a
      controlled sample) -- DM has no mechanism for it.  This is the sharp discriminator.
    - Wide binaries: F(Q)Theta's exponential gamma_v (~1.03-1.06) is TOO CLOSE to Newton to separate
      cleanly with DR4; and it lies BELOW the registered nu_RAR Arm A band (1.16-1.23).  So DR4 wide
      binaries chiefly test WHICH KERNEL is right: a confirmed gamma_v~1.2 (Chae/Arm A) would DISFAVOUR
      the exponential F(Q)Theta kernel (favouring nu_RAR); a Newton-leaning result is consistent with it.

======================================================================================================================
  SUMMARY: 15/15 checks PASS.
  STATEMENT: 'F(Q)Theta predicts a nonzero, kernel-specific EFE (SEP violation) -- wide-binary
             gamma_v ~ 1.03(can)/1.06(alt), below the registered nu_RAR Arm A band; a ~2x dwarf
             sigma-R_gc correlation -- while dark matter predicts exactly zero for both.'
  VERDICT: PASS (statement TRUE)
